@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: why the in-container prep is a Go subprocess and what it therefore cannot hand the agent
' covers: cmd/proveo-entrypoint/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: internal/entrypoint/**
' covers: internal/contract/contract_test.go (TestEntrypointsRunTheShellPreludeThenPrep)
' covers: internal/contract/env_prelude_test.go (TestPrepKeepsOnlyWhatCrossesTheBoundary)
'
' ── N22 + N24 (DONE (wt) 2026-10-17): prep IS THE ONE RUNTIME-USER AND GIT-CONTEXT
' STEP, IN EVERY IMAGE, AND HAS NO SMOKE MODE ─────────────────────────────────
' MEASURED, cmd/proveo-entrypoint/main.go:
'   usage  "prep | verify [dir] | adb-mirror" (:17); `prep` takes NO argument —
'          an extra one prints usage and exits 2 (:48-51)
'   prep   entrypoint.EnsureRuntimeUser() then reportGitContext() (:53-54);
'          nothing else
' internal/entrypoint holds EnsureRuntimeUser and firstNonEmpty only: SmokeReady,
' its hourly sleep loop and the target argument are DELETED (N22 [rec]) — every
' def had cleared PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST before calling prep, so none of it ever ran.
' Every def entrypoint runs `proveo-entrypoint prep || true`; the
' `env PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST=` prefix and `export PROVEO_SMOKE_TARGET=` are gone.
' Smoke mode is the def's own run_smoke_test (entrypoint-lib.sh:174, plus the
' sentinel lines opencode and hermes print themselves), unchanged.
' N24: entrypoint-lib.sh no longer defines ensure_runtime_user or
' report_git_context — the Go pair is the ONLY implementation. The [rec] was
' blocked because hermes (FROM nousresearch/hermes-agent) shipped no
' proveo-entrypoint; the user chose "Ship prep into hermes (Recommended)", so
' defs/hermes/Dockerfile builds it in a stage of its own
' (_spec/defs/hermes/hermes-topology.puml) and defs/hermes/entrypoint.sh:11-14
' runs the same prelude-then-prep as every def. The lib's top-level HOME
' fallback (entrypoint-lib.sh:4-6) stays: it is not a twin of anything.
' Tests: TestPrepTakesNoTargetAndNoSmokeMode (env_prelude_test.go:177);
' TestEntrypointsRunTheShellPreludeThenPrep (contract_test.go:63, hermes
' included, the smoke prefix banned); TestPrepIsTheOnlyRuntimeUserAndGitContextStep
' (contract_test.go:104 — no shell twins, hermes ships proveo-entrypoint).
' [Unverified] image builds for this change were still running when recorded.
'
' ── N1 (DONE (wt) 2026-10-17): prep KEEPS ONLY WHAT CROSSES THE BOUNDARY ───
' Part of the user's "apply fixes for SEC2, SEC3, N1, F18, …" (repo-simplification.puml
' N1, option 1). MEASURED then: `proveo-entrypoint prep [target]` ran EnsureRuntimeUser
' (the passwd entry), the git-context report and the smoke sentinel, nothing else;
' internal/entrypoint held only EnsureRuntimeUser, SmokeReady and firstNonEmpty
' (N22 has since removed the smoke half). The exec mode
' (`proveo-entrypoint <target> -- cmd`) is deleted. BridgeGoogleKeys, BridgeGitIdentity,
' NormalizeModel and ApplyEnvBridges are deleted with their tests, and so is the
' chdir. Every process-local step is the SHELL's now: each def entrypoint runs
' set_working_directory, bridge_google_keys and bridge_git_identity, then
' `proveo-entrypoint prep` (e.g. defs/codex/entrypoint.sh:12-16); the `else`
' branches for an image without the binary are gone.
' FLAGGED (image agent; consequences to confirm, recorded not decided here):
'   * the ORDER is reversed — the shell prelude runs BEFORE prep, so prep's git
'     report sees the working directory and identity the shell set;
'   * agents now RECEIVE the git-identity env — bridge_git_identity exports in
'     the shell the agent inherits, where its Go twin exported into a dying child.
' Pinned by TestEntrypointsRunTheShellPreludeThenPrep and
' TestPrepKeepsOnlyWhatCrossesTheBoundary. After the review fixes the images were
' rebuilt from the tree and all 7 TestImage* pass (reported).
title proveo-entrypoint prep — only what crosses the process boundary

node "Agent container" as CTR <<host>> {

  component "defs/<name>/entrypoint.sh\n(PID 1 shell — execs the agent)" as SH <<app>>

  frame "In-shell prelude (FIRST)\nentrypoint-lib.sh" as SHELLPRE {
    component "set_working_directory\nchdir(2)" as CWD <<app>>
    component "bridge_google_keys\nGoogle key alias exports" as ENV <<app>>
    component "bridge_git_identity\nGIT_CONFIG_KEY_n exports" as GITID <<app>>
  }

  component "proveo-entrypoint prep\n(child process, AFTER the prelude;\nno argument, every def incl. hermes)" as PREP <<app>>

  frame "Crosses the boundary\n(external to the process)" as OK {
    component "EnsureRuntimeUser\npasswd entry + writable HOME" as UID <<app>>
    component "git-context report\nstdout preamble" as GITCTX <<app>>
  }

  component "run_smoke_test\n(the def's own, under PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST=1)" as SMOKE <<async>>

  component "agent CLI\n(inherits the SHELL's env + cwd)" as AGENT <<app>>
}

SH ARROW_MAIN SHELLPRE : sourced lib, same process
SH ARROW_MAIN PREP : " ""proveo-entrypoint prep || true"" "
PREP ARROW_MAIN OK : effects outlive the child
SH ARROW_OPTIONAL SMOKE : smoke mode, after its own preamble
SHELLPRE ARROW_MAIN AGENT : cwd + exports inherited
SH ARROW_MAIN AGENT : " ""exec <agent> \"$@\""" "

note right of SHELLPRE
  **A child cannot mutate its parent.**
  ""chdir"" and ""setenv"" are per-process, so every
  step that sets them runs IN the shell the agent
  inherits. HISTORY: prep ran them too, exited 0, and
  the effects died with it — silently.
end note

note bottom of SH
  **Contract for def entrypoints.** Source the lib,
  run the prelude (""set_working_directory <dir>"",
  ""bridge_google_keys"", ""bridge_git_identity"") and the
  harness's own model bridge, THEN call ""prep"". Each
  fills only unset slots, so ""sbx run -e"" or
  ""--env-file"" values win. No step loads a workspace
  "".env"" (N7). See _spec/packages/lib/steps.puml.
end note

note top of SMOKE
  **Smoke mode is the def's, not prep's.** prep's
  own smoke mode never ran: every def cleared
  ""PROVEO_SMOKE_TEST"" before calling it, so the
  sentinel always came from ""run_smoke_test"" at the
  end of the def's preamble. N22 deleted prep's copy.
end note

note bottom of PREP
  **prep is the shared Go half, and only the half that can be.**
  Runtime user and git-context report — effects that live outside the
  process, with no shell twin (N24). HISTORY: it also bridged the Google
  keys, applied env bridges, bridged git identity and chdir'd (deleted with
  N1, 2026-10-17), had a smoke mode and a target argument (deleted with
  N22), loaded the workspace "".env"" (deleted with N7) and wrote the
  credential sentinel (deleted with D1, 2026-10-16).

  **Non-secret preferences travel by value** — the model and UI preferences
  from the shared baseline plus the harness's own ""config:"" list, as Kit
  environment. Secrets are declared in ""env:"" and travel through sbx's
  secret store instead.
end note

@enduml
